@startbpmn BP04_CaptureAndCurateIdeas
lang en

output L1 "01_detailed/BP04_CaptureAndCurateIdeas.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP04_CaptureAndCurateIdeas.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - an idea has 0..1 theme; theme-less is legitimate and grouped under Unthemed: BR-03
'   - an archived idea cannot be edited: BR-05
'   - the hand-made order is a grouping convenience with no funnel consequence: BR-88
'   - archiving an idea archives the projects that came from it, on informed approval: BR-112, QB-42
'   - deleting an idea cascades its projects with approval, or the deletion is rejected: BR-14, QB-41
'   - detaching a project to parentless is deliberately not offered: BR-14, BR-21
'   - an idea owns no board: the selectables consequence belongs to the project the cascade
'     archives, and is drawn once, in BP17 where the project is the subject. Here the rule is
'     bound to the archiving step and no step draws it: BR-43, BR-112, SA 2026-10-14
'   - the capture is opportunistic and happens during execution: section 1.2 step 3
'
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms included: the field drafts as it is filled in, and the
'     operation that keeps it is drawn ONCE, in BP19, not per editing process. Here it is a
'     bound rule on the step that fills the field: BR-121, SA 2026-10-11
'   - an archived item cannot be edited, idea and notes alike: BR-05
'   - one editor per entity serves writing an idea down and changing one alike, and nothing
'     separated the two chains but the fields they stored, so they are ONE request: UX-04,
'     SA 2026-10-11. Call site BP04.03 (Amend an idea) is RETIRED, its id never reused
'   - a step never enumerates the fields an editor stores: which fields the idea carries is a
'     Detail Design matter and is not known yet, so the step says "Store the edit" rather than
'     naming a title and a theme affiliation: SA 2026-10-14
'   - the notes are a field of the one idea editor, not an editor of their own: writing them is
'     part of editing the idea and submitting is the commit, so call site BP04.10 (Commit the
'     idea notes) is RETIRED and its id never reused: UX-04, DRW-12, SA 2026-10-14, ADR-066
'   - the filter and the ordering in force are remembered interface state with no request of
'     their own, so no step draws changing them; the read states that it answers what they
'     admit: BR-88, BR-92, SA 2026-10-14
'   - the box carries the act's own word, not the generic edit: the user CAPTURES an idea, DEFINES
'     a goal on one and CREATES a project on one - a seam is an act, not an opening: SA 2026-10-16
'   - NOTHING IS FETCHED HERE. Every record is loaded once, at start-up (BP01), so a step that only
'     went to the store is gone, and one that selects or qualifies what the act works on says so
'     instead of saying read. What a chain still asks the system for is what it COMPUTES, which is
'     business and stays out of the client. When data is read is a detail design decision:
'     BR-128, DRW-14, SA 2026-10-17 ("when we will read data is not a business concern, but a
'     detail design decision ... I rule that this will be done once at startup")
'
' Call-site collapsing: re-affiliating an idea to a theme is a field of the amend request, not a
' chain of its own, and so are the notes: one editor per entity, one submit, one request.

' A seam into another process is drawn as one step that asks the system for nothing, with a note
' saying whose business it is, and the hub takes the user back afterwards. DRW-02 makes the seam
' significant, and BP17 and BP09 already drew theirs; the rest of the set did not, which is the
' asymmetry F-3 recorded. Swept on SA 2026-10-16 ("still can't find any checkout action on the
' diagram").
'
pool "User" {
  start "An idea worth keeping, or a list worth tidying"
  :Work an idea;
  rule BR-118

  if "What needs doing?" then "write one down, or change one"
    :Capture the idea;
    rule BR-121
    note "What is typed drafts as it is filled in, the notes included, and the draft survives a crash and a restart. Submitting is the commit."
    :Submit the idea;
    send "Edit an idea" to editIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as recorded
    note "A theme is optional, and a theme-less idea is grouped under Unthemed. An archived idea is not editable."
    end "Idea recorded"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "group related ones together"
    :Order an idea;
    send "Reorder ideas" to reorderIn
    receive "The ordering outcome" as reordered
    note "The order groups related ideas. It carries no priority."
    end "Ideas ordered"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "park one"
    :Archive an idea;
    send "See what archiving an idea takes" to archImpactIn
    receive "What the archiving will take" as archImpact
    if "Approve what the archiving takes?" rule BR-112 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the archiving;
      send "Archive an idea" to archiveIn
      receive "The archiving outcome" as archived
    else "reject"
      end "Archiving abandoned"
    endif
    end "Idea set aside"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "drop one for good"
    :Delete an idea;
    send "See what deleting an idea takes" to delImpactIn
    receive "What the deletion will take" as delImpact
    if "Approve what the deletion takes?" rule BR-14 then "approve"
      :Select a valid cascading option;
      rule BR-19
      :Confirm the deletion;
      send "Delete an idea" to deleteIn
      receive "The deletion outcome" as deleted
    else "reject"
      end "Deletion abandoned"
    endif
    end "Idea deleted"
  elseif "What needs doing?" then "commit to one"
    :Define a goal on the idea;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the goal;
    send "Define a goal" to goalIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as goalDefined
    note "The goal's editor opens on the idea, with the idea already linked. A goal needs a theme, so one defined on a theme-less idea is refused with its reason. Maintaining the goal afterwards is its own process (BP05)."
    end "Goal defined"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "start work on one"
    :Create a project on the idea;
    rule BR-121
    :Submit the project;
    send "Create a project" to projectIn
    receive "The editing outcome" as projectCreated
    note "A project carries one optional parent, and the idea is it here. Working its board (BP11), or laying its course out (BP18), is its own process."
    end "Project created"

  elseif "What needs doing?" then "look at the archived ones"
    :Open the archived ideas (BP15);
    note "The archive is reached by an explicit act. Reading it, bringing one back and destroying one out of it are its own process (BP15)."
    end "Archive opened"
  endif
}

system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Idea submitted" as editIn
  call "BP04.02_EditIdea" "Edit an idea" {
    :Store the edit;
    rule BR-03
    rule BR-05
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to recorded
  note "The theme may be absent. An archived idea is not editable."
  end "Idea answered"

  messageStart "Idea reordering requested" as reorderIn
  call "BP04.05_ReorderIdeas" "Reorder ideas" {
    :Apply the new order;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The ordering outcome" to reordered
  end "Reordering answered"

  messageStart "Archiving impact requested" as archImpactIn
  call "BP04.06_ReadTheArchivingImpact" "See what archiving an idea takes" {
    :Report what the archiving will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-112
  }
  send "What the archiving will take" to archImpact
  note "Nothing below a project can be left behind, so the gesture is approve-or-abandon."
  end "Archiving impact answered"

  messageStart "Idea archiving requested" as archiveIn
  call "BP04.07_ArchiveIdea" "Archive an idea" {
    :Archive confirmed items;
    rule BR-112
    rule BR-43
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The archiving outcome" to archived
  note "Unarchiving restores the whole bundle."
  end "Archiving answered"

  messageStart "Deletion impact requested" as delImpactIn
  call "BP04.08_ReadTheDeletionImpact" "See what deleting an idea takes" {
    :Report what the deletion will take, and what of it can be declined;
    rule BR-12
    rule BR-14
    rule BR-19
    rule BR-117
  }
  send "What the deletion will take" to delImpact
  note "Keeping a project behind is not offered. A goal that links the idea survives minus the link."
  end "Deletion impact answered"

  messageStart "Idea deletion requested" as deleteIn
  call "BP04.09_DeleteIdea" "Delete an idea" {
    :Delete confirmed items;
    rule BR-14
    :Unlink the idea from every goal that links it;
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The deletion outcome" to deleted
  note "A goal left with no linked idea is flagged on its current state."
  end "Deletion answered"

  messageStart "Goal submitted" as goalIn
  call "BP04.11_DefineGoal" "Define a goal" {
    if "Does the goal name a theme?" rule BR-01 then "yes"
      :Store the edit;
      rule BR-04
      rule BR-08
    else "no"
      :Refuse it and say why;
      rule BR-84
    endif
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to goalDefined
  note "The idea comes in as one of the ideas behind the goal. A theme-less idea gives the goal no theme, and a goal without one is refused, which is the same answer the Goals view's own editor gives."
  end "Goal answered"

  messageStart "Project submitted" as projectIn
  call "BP04.12_CreateProject" "Create a project" {
    :Store the edit;
    rule BR-96
    rule BR-97
    :Give a new project its own column template;
    rule BR-108
    :Give it what its kind brings: one board where it is simple, an empty plan where it is activity-based;
    rule BR-101
    rule BR-111
    :Report the outcome;
  }
  send "The editing outcome" to projectCreated
  note "The parent is the idea, carried in from where the user started. The kind is declared once and for the project's life."
  end "Project answered"
}

@endbpmn
